---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PlaygroundEmbed from '../components/PlaygroundEmbed.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Web Playground — Be Insiculous"
  description="Insiculous 2D Web Playground: the scene editor running in the browser on WebGPU with local IndexedDB persistence."
>
  <p class="section-label">the editor</p>
  <h1>Web Playground</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The Insiculous 2D scene editor running entirely in the browser on WebGPU.
    Build scenes, test physics and behaviors, and work with projects stored
    in your browser’s IndexedDB.
  </p>

  <PlaygroundEmbed />

  <section>
    <h2>Browser persistence</h2>
    <p>
      Projects and scenes are saved into your browser’s IndexedDB storage.
      When you press <kbd>Ctrl+S</kbd> to save a scene, modified files are
      committed locally. The bundled samples provide a starting point; if you
      ever wish to discard local edits, use the <em>Reset to bundled</em> button
      to restore the original version.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Command API</h2>
    <p>
      The editor exposes its command interface to the browser through WebAssembly.
      You can inspect entities and scene state using commands like <code>list</code> directly
      in the console above.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  kbd {
    background: var(--surface-raised, #222);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-bright);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
</style>
